# Line endings. Every text file in the index uses LF (measured: 8119 text files i/lf, none i/crlf). The oracle tests compare scene
# text, including the CR bytes inside Script url strings, with recordings made from LF files. A Windows checkout with the system
# setting core.autocrlf=true wrote CRLF into every .wrl fixture, so every Windows comparison of scene text differed by "\r\n"
# against "\n" (Windows runner, 2026-11-04). This rule gives the working tree LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says.
* text=auto eol=lf

